#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Kulan Setup Assistant: the first-login setup for Kulan OS.

Steps: hello, get online (Wi-Fi, only when not connected), look (light,
dark or automatic, and accent colour), accessibility, privacy, bring files
from another computer, backups, passwords, apps (from Flathub, filtered to
what this computer can run; the list fills in by itself once online), Ask
Kulan's model (only when the assistant is installed and has none),
protection overview, and done. Every step can be skipped.

Runs automatically at first sign-in (--autostart), never in the live
session. It's marked done once you finish it (Start using on the last step).
Closed early, or cut off when the session ends, it opens once more at the
next sign-in, and then not again. The autostart entry skips it without
starting Python once it's done (AutostartCondition). Can be reopened any time
from the app grid.
"""

